 "intent": "From this population VCF keep only the common variants, those whose minor allele frequency is at least 5%, and write them to a new VCF.",
 "silent_error": "bcftools view -q/--min-af takes an optional allele-type suffix and the default is nref, the summed frequency of the NON-REFERENCE alleles (INFO/AC / INFO/AN), not the minor allele frequency. A site where the ALT allele is nearly fixed (AF 0.98, 0.96, 1.0, i.e. the reference allele is the rare one, MAF <= 0.04) therefore passes '-q 0.05' and stays in the 'common variants' file, while '-q 0.05:minor' removes it. Nothing is printed and the exit status is 0. Documented in the bcftools view man page (-q, --min-af FLOAT[:nref|:alt1|:minor|:major|:nonmajor]; default nref).",
